Here is the commit message:
net/sched: act_gate: snapshot parameters with RCU on replace

The gate action can be replaced while the hrtimer callback or dump path is
walking the schedule list.

Convert the parameters to an RCU-protected snapshot and swap updates under
tcf_lock, freeing the previous snapshot via call_rcu(). When REPLACE omits
the entry list, preserve the existing schedule so the effective state is
unchanged.

Fixes: a51c328df310 ("net: qos: introduce a gate control flow action")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Paul Moses <p@1g4.org>
Tested-by: Vladimir Oltean <vladimir.oltean@nxp.com>
Acked-by: Jamal Hadi Salim <jhs@mojatatu.com>
Reviewed-by: Victor Nogueira <victor@mojatatu.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260223150512.2251594-2-p@1g4.org
Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>

Here is the root cause:
The gate action's parameters, including the schedule list (`struct tcf_gate_params`), were directly modified in-place during a REPLACE operation while the hrtimer callback (`gate_timer_func`) or the dump path (`tcf_gate_dump`) could be concurrently accessing the same data without synchronization, leading to a use-after-free or data corruption.

Here is the patch:
